Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 11:28:37 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1041/1286] The Collection: a fourth tab, workspaces, many
 takes at once, the trash in the page

- Collection (heresy-collection.js): every take as a tile or a row; search with * and ?;
  filters by how it was made (generated, imported, regenerated, re-rendered) and by what is made
  from it (stems, debuzz, remaster, upscale); sort; favourites; workspaces as in SUNO (made,
  renamed, deleted with a double click; takes stay); hidden takes (out of every list, not
  deleted). Ticks with Shift for a range and "select all shown"; together: favourite, add to or
  take out of a workspace, hide or show, export a ZIP (FLAC or WAV, with or without what is made
  from them; built on Forge, saved by the browser), move to the trash.
- The trash: what went there, since when, how big; give back; delete for good (asks first); an
  automatic empty after 7, 14 or 28 days, off until chosen.
- The header holds the workspace in hand: the takes list shows only it and new takes land in it.
- The takes list has a quick search (the same wildcards) and leaves hidden takes out.
The lab keeps the marks in yue2_os/collection.json and the trash in trash/DATE/TAKE.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
